<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arbogast</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 394</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Flavius Arbogastes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arbogast was a Frankish general in the Roman army who became the dominant figure at the western court of the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-ii">Valentinian II</a>. After Valentinian's death in 392 he raised the rhetorician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a> as emperor, but their army was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus">Battle of the Frigidus</a> in 394, and Arbogast took his own life.</p></div>
